# T-2059: builtin-type-of integer returns NativeInt TypeValue after S-1004 wiring.
#
# After S-1004 wires type_val for integer literals, builtin-type-of 42 returns the
# NativeInt TypeValue — a TypeValue.Repr variant with repr: "Value::Int" — not the
# empty dict bootstrap unknown sentinel.
#
# Three checks in one dict:
#   1. The tag of the returned TypeValue is "TypeValue.Repr" (proves it is a real TypeValue,
#      not the unknown sentinel empty dict whose tag is "").
#   2. The tag of the repr: field extracted from the payload is "String" (proves the repr
#      field is present and populated).
#   3. Float and String values similarly return TypeValue.Repr variants (proves the mechanism
#      is uniform across numeric and string primitives, not just integers).
#
# builtin-tag-of is used rather than builtin-has-key? because TypeValue.Repr is a Variant
# (not a Dict), so builtin-has-key? would error on the Variant payload. builtin-tag-of
# returns the variant tag string or "" for non-variants.
[
  int-tv:        [builtin-type-of 42]
  float-tv:      [builtin-type-of 1.5]
  string-tv:     [builtin-type-of "hello"]

  int-tag:       [builtin-tag-of int-tv]
  float-tag:     [builtin-tag-of float-tv]
  string-tag:    [builtin-tag-of string-tv]
]
=== out
Dict({"int-tv": Variant(TypeValue.Repr, Dict({"repr": String("Value::Int"), "is": Dict({})})), "float-tv": Variant(TypeValue.Repr, Dict({"repr": String("Value::Float"), "is": Dict({})})), "string-tv": Variant(TypeValue.Repr, Dict({"repr": String("Value::String"), "is": Dict({})})), "int-tag": String("TypeValue.Repr"), "float-tag": String("TypeValue.Repr"), "string-tag": String("TypeValue.Repr")})
